# The first message the DB-bundled OCI client sends in proxy mode, captured off
# the wire from sqlplus 23.26 (the client inside gvenzl/oracle-free:23-slim)
# against a dbbat proxy, immediately after AUTH completed.
#
# These are the bytes of the TNS Data packet *payload*: two data-flag bytes,
# then the TTC message. Recorded while reproducing
# specs/.../2026-08-12-12-bundled-oci-client-refused-and-hung-under-a-restrictive-grant.md,
# so the unit half of that fix needs no Oracle container.
#
# 00 00        data flags
# 11           TTC piggyback message type (dbbat's TTCFuncOFETCH — see ttc.go)
# 6b           TTC function code: an OCI session piggyback dbbat has no reading for
# 04           the PIGGYBACK's sequence number — not the call's
# ...          a body of 8-byte little-endian fields dbbat cannot walk
# 03 3b 05     the call the client is actually parked on, stapled behind it,
#              sequence 5
#
# Read bytes 1..3 as a big-endian cursor id, the way the since-deleted
# decodeOFETCH did, and you get 0x6b04 = 27396: the "untracked cursor" this
# frame used to be refused as.
0000116b0400000000000005000000000000003a0000003775000001000000033b050000000000000600000000000000fefffffffffffffff401000000000000fefffffffffffffffeffffffffffffff0100000000000000
